---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="DeepAnnotate — JD">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/projects" class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">← Back to Projects</a>
  </div>

  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">DeepAnnotate</h1>

  <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
    <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-medium" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Completed</span>
    <a href="https://github.com/Jagruth07/Deepannotate_repo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm">GitHub →</a>
  </div>

  <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
    DeepAnnotate is a full-stack, unified mobile application prototype designed for efficiently 
    collecting diverse data types (audio, images, and video) from distributed users. It features 
    an integrated Admin Dashboard and User Interface, completely removing the need for a separate website.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Tech Stack</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Flutter</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Dart</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Node.js</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Express</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Socket.io</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">PostgreSQL</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">AWS S3</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Key Features</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-[var(--color-muted)] space-y-2">
      <li>Unified Flutter app housing both Admin Dashboard and User interfaces</li>
      <li>Real-time live feed via WebSockets (Socket.io)</li>
      <li>Direct AWS S3 uploads with pre-signed URLs</li>
      <li>Global dark/light mode toggle</li>
      <li>Offline task tracking with completion status</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Architecture</h2>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      The project transitioned from Firebase to an industry-standard scalable architecture. 
      The Node.js Express backend handles API requests and WebSocket connections, while PostgreSQL 
      stores task and user data. All media submissions are uploaded directly from the Flutter app 
      to an AWS S3 bucket using pre-signed HTTP PUT URLs, keeping cloud credentials securely isolated 
      on the backend.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
